**Current annotation queue (2026-10-07):** 6,112 grouped catchall dictionary tasks
covering 8,337 forms, with 0 pending contextual homonym tasks. Exported in batches
of at most 500; import and regenerate after each batch to reuse family decisions.
Current workflow and verification: [docs/mixed_harmony_catchall_workflow.md](docs/mixed_harmony_catchall_workflow.md).

However, the broader check found unresolved cases outside those queues:

- **Partially resolved 2026-10-07:** of the 15,996 unreviewed native-labelled mixed-harmony forms,
  7,173 whose native and loanword conversion branches agree now convert automatically during training export.
  Of the 8,823 origin-dependent forms, 111 across 36 families were recovered from existing direct human reviews,
  preserving human spellings, variants, and source/analyzer provenance. After that recovery, 8,712 forms remained
  excluded from annotation queues and training export. All pre-existing review rows were retained unchanged.
  After recovery, all 47,259 reviewed words and 479 variants pass dictionary validation.
  Entries, validation, manifest, and full database backup: [docs/mixed_harmony_family_recovery.md](docs/mixed_harmony_family_recovery.md).
- **Source corrected 2026-10-07:** the user confirmed all ten flagged hyphen boundaries were internal word breaks.
  All eleven occurrences were joined in both source sentences and token annotations, preserving case, punctuation,
  labels, and token indices. Human review tables were unchanged. The exclusion count is now 8,704 unique forms,
  including 827 hyphenated forms. Original-row backup and occurrence list:
  [docs/hyphen_boundary_source_corrections.md](docs/hyphen_boundary_source_corrections.md).
- **Recovery audited 2026-10-07 (read-only):** 371 compounds have existing component/family evidence;
  an experimental deterministic-suffix check adds 95 forms and 10 compounds, preserving ten human corrections.
  The 476 candidates cover 1,596 occurrences and would leave 8,228 excluded if recovered; the actual count
  was 8,704 at audit time. Boundary clues hold out 54 compounds. Converter tracing also found 29 forms that silently
  omit conditional letters despite producing nonempty Latin output. No source, reviews, or conversion rules changed.
  Evidence, limitations, candidate spellings, and reproduction: [docs/mixed_harmony_recovery_audit.md](docs/mixed_harmony_recovery_audit.md).
- **Compounds recovered 2026-10-07:** the authorized first tier recovered 371 compounds / 748 occurrences
  using reviewed, deterministic, and existing safe-family components, with complete component provenance.
  The remaining 8,333 forms, including all 105 expanded-rule candidates, stay excluded. All pre-existing
  source and review rows were preserved. Loaders reject stale component evidence; direct human reviews dominate.
  Backup, manifest, validation, and all spellings: [docs/mixed_harmony_compound_recovery.md](docs/mixed_harmony_compound_recovery.md).
- **Catchall enabled 2026-10-07:** the remaining native-labelled mixed-vowel forms now enter annotation.
  Converter fixes make 51 of the former 8,333 forms origin-independent; 8,282 still require review.
  Separate hyphen component conversion exposes 55 additional dependent forms. Safe expanded suffix
  propagation and direct-human-over-derived precedence support frequent small imports. Of 29 audited
  silent omissions, 28 now have complete proposals; the unresolved fragment stays blank for human review.
  All 371 recovered approvals remain valid; exporting changed no database rows.
- **Resolved 2026-10-07:** all 114 stored `HAMZA` reviews were migrated to preserved `ʼ` (U+02BC) spellings.
  Preferred policy: preserve hamza wherever possible. All other reviewed text and origins were retained.
  At that migration, all 47,148 reviewed words and 478 reviewed variants passed dictionary validation.
  Original entries, migrated spellings, and backup location: [docs/hamza_stored_reviews.md](docs/hamza_stored_reviews.md).
  Converter updated 2026-10-07: verified hamza families preserve `ʼ` deterministically in both origin branches, suffix forms, and hyphenated components; the retired DSL/project stays removed.

Earlier completion counts covered the exported queues only. So the current projects are complete, but I can’t yet confirm that the entire dataset needs no further review or cleanup.

